<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Volunteer Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chinese People's Volunteers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> was the force of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> that fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>. Sent into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> in October 1950 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peng-dehuai">Peng Dehuai</a>, it drove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> forces back from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yalu-river">Yalu River</a> and fought them to a stalemate before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> of July 1953, at the cost of hundreds of thousands of Chinese dead. The last units left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> in 1958.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-volunteer-army.jpg" alt="People's Volunteer Army" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georgezh9617 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B8%AD%E5%9B%BD%E4%BA%BA%E6%B0%91%E5%BF%97%E6%84%BF%E5%86%9B%E8%83%B8%E7%AB%A0.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
